
Discussed the advantages of glb files with Copilot. Removed some blend files from repository and replaced them with obj and glb files. Wrote a python script to prepare a blender character for export.

Organized project to work with multiple operating systems and git. Added a Makefile to work with g++ on unix systems. Added flags to compile for unix on windows with MSYS2. New make command: g++ -c main.cpp -o main -std=c++17 -Wall -mwin32 -lGL -lGLU -lGLEW -lglfw. Added the fopen function for unix instead of fopen_s for windows. This is a temporary solution. The fstream function needs to be used to be compatible with both systems. Re-organized project folder to work out of git repository. Started a new project in Visual Studio and placed GitHub repository inside the folder. Downloaded git and set up commits through terminal: cd to local repository directory (now inside visual studio project folder). downloading: git clone https://github.com/door1derive/AntecededAftermath.git ./. uploading: git init; git add .; git commit -m "commit name"; git status; git branch -M main; git remote add door1derive AntecededAftermath; git push -u origin main.

Updated main.py load function. Changed unsigned ints to signed ints for window width/height to be compatible with glfw. Added float flags to prevent conversion from double. Defaulted GL array sizes to 1 for compatability with Windows.
